      "writtenOn": "2015-12-17T14:11:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In https://golang.org/doc/asm#directives , the paragraph right under the method code snippet: \"In the general case, the frame size is followed by an argument size, separated by a minus sign. (It\u0027s not a subtraction, just idiosyncratic syntax.) The frame size $24-8 states that the function has a 24-byte frame and is called with 8 bytes of argument, which live on the caller\u0027s frame\".\n\nI interpreted the above that the stack is 200 bytes beside the 8 byte argument passed in, but looking at it again I can see it probably means 200 bytes, *out of which* 8 are the params. Just to verify, is the later the correct interpretation?",
      "parentUuid": "c50c9af0_191ccb4f",
      "revId": "7158f220ba515d934c55f56e2e2d5908d7ddd875",
